```

Drawing: for each pixel, compute:
- alpha of the rounded-rectangle SDF (bg): corner radius r. Standard SDF: box with rounded corners.
- pulse polyline SDF with a stroke.
- Apple icon: full-bleed square (no rounding).

Pulse path for 512: baseline y=290; points:
(88, 290) → (178, 290) → (226, 176) → (286, 372) → (334, 290) → (424, 290)
Stroke width 30, round caps.

Hmm, wait — with bg #F7F6F3 and ink #111, the icon will look like a minimal pulse line — perfect for "Rhythm".

SDF for line segment: distance from point p to segment ab.
Round cap: distance to segment already includes caps. Smooth AA: coverage = clamp(0.5 + (w/2 - d)/aa, 0, 1), aa=1.5.

Rounded-rect SDF:
```
function sdRoundRect(px, py, cx, cy, hw, hh, r) {
  const qx = Math.abs(px - cx) - (hw - r)
  const qy = Math.abs(py - cy) - (hh - r)
  const dx = Math.max(qx, 0), dy = Math.max(qy, 0)
  return Math.min(Math.max(qx, qy), 0) + Math.hypot(dx, dy) - r
}
```
Full bleed: hw=hh=256, r=115 (22.5%). Maskable safe zone: motif is within the central 80% (368px) — my pulse spans x 88..424 (width 336, ~66%), y 176..372 (196, 38%) — within safe zone (central 80% = 51.2..460.8 x). Good.

Colors: bg = #F7F6F3 = (247,246,243), ink #111111.
Apple: same but without the rounded-rect alpha (all opaque).

Sizes: 512 (icon-512.png, also maskable), 192 (icon-192.png), 180 (apple-touch-icon.png). Scale the geometry by size/512.

favicon: keep the template's favicon.svg? Replace with my own simple SVG (pulse on bone). The template has a public/favicon.svg (Vite logo) and public/icons.svg (Vite icons sprite) — remove icons.svg, replace favicon.svg with my own pulse mark.

